# CMS22 Blood Pressure Screening — measure caseload

// A clinical scenario where a patient at a routine annual wellness visit
// has their blood pressure measured and the reading is normal. The
// patient satisfies the CMS22 Numerator via the Normal BP Reading path.

library "CMS22 Blood Pressure Screening".
covers "CMS22".


// ============ Patient facts ============

fact "Maria Garcia":
- name is "Maria Garcia".
- birth date is "1972-08-22".
- defined by "Patient".


// ============ Clinical facts ============

fact "Annual Wellness Visit":
- code is "G0438".
- date is "2026-03-10".
- defined by "CMS22 Asserted"."BP Screening Encounters".

fact "Normal BP Panel":
- code is "85354-9".
- date is "2026-03-10".
- defined by "CMS22 Asserted"."Blood Pressure Panels".

fact "Normal Systolic Component":
- code is "8480-6".
- date is "2026-03-10".
- value is 118.
- defined by "CMS22 Asserted"."Systolic Blood Pressure Code".

fact "Normal Diastolic Component":
- code is "8462-4".
- date is "2026-03-10".
- value is 76.
- defined by "CMS22 Asserted"."Diastolic Blood Pressure Code".


// ============ Cases ============

case "Maria has normal BP at her wellness visit":
- description is `Maria's last systolic and diastolic readings on her
  qualifying encounter day are both below the Normal-BP thresholds (118/76).
  She satisfies the Numerator via the Normal BP Reading path.`.
- subject is "Maria Garcia".
- fact is "Annual Wellness Visit".
- fact is "Normal BP Panel".
- fact is "Normal Systolic Component".
- fact is "Normal Diastolic Component".
- result is "Initial Population" is true.
- result is "Numerator" is true.
